00:02:31.551 --> 00:02:33.118
Because, as he later clarified,

00:02:33.218 --> 00:02:34.954
it was the judge's
Mexican heritage

00:02:35.054 --> 00:02:37.256
that made him unfit
to judge Trump.

00:02:37.657 --> 00:02:39.592 line:0%
You're invoking his race
when talking about whether

00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:41.361 line:0%
-or not he can do his job.
-Here's what I'm saying.

00:02:41.461 --> 00:02:44.563 line:0%
Jack, I'm building a wall, okay?
I'm building a wall.

00:02:44.663 --> 00:02:46.499 line:0%
I'm trying to keep business
out of Mexico.

00:02:46.599 --> 00:02:47.633 line:0%
Mexico's fine.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:49.735 line:0%
-There's nothing-- A Mexican--
-But he's an American.

00:02:49.935 --> 00:02:52.271 line:0%
Uh, he's of Mexican heritage,
and he's very proud of it,

00:02:52.371 --> 00:02:54.339 line:0%
-as I am where I come from.
-But he--

00:02:54.439 --> 00:02:55.707
-Wait...
-(AUDIENCE LAUGH)

00:02:55.808 --> 00:02:58.877
-Where exactly are you from?
-(AUDIENCE LAUGH)

00:02:58.977 --> 00:03:01.380
Because you look like
you came out of a clogged drain

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:03.149
-at the Wonka factory.
-(AUDIENCE LAUGH AND APPLAUD)

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:04.984
And, you know what?
That's great!

00:03:05.084 --> 00:03:06.619
I think that's fine.

00:03:07.153 --> 00:03:10.389
But think about
what he's implying there.

00:03:10.489 --> 00:03:12.658
The judge is unfit to do his job

00:03:12.758 --> 00:03:14.560
because of
his ethnic background.

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:17.429
And just his morning,
Trump took it a step further.

00:03:17.763 --> 00:03:19.899 line:0%
What if he was a Muslim though?
You've had-- been very tough

00:03:19.999 --> 00:03:21.600 line:0%
on temporary Muslim
immigration ban.

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:23.736 line:0%
If it were a Muslim judge,
would you also feel like

00:03:23.836 --> 00:03:25.538 line:0%
they wouldn't be able
to treat you fairly,

00:03:25.638 --> 00:03:27.139 line:0%
because of that policy of yours?

00:03:27.239 --> 00:03:28.707 line:0%
Uh... It's possible, yes.

00:03:28.807 --> 00:03:30.410 line:0%
Yeah, that would be possible,
absolutely.

00:03:30.743 --> 00:03:33.946
I would say that was the
dictionary definition of bigotry

00:03:34.046 --> 00:03:36.782
except after this campaign,
the definition of bigotry

00:03:36.883 --> 00:03:39.585
might just become,
"See: Trump comma Donald."

00:03:39.852 --> 00:03:42.088
-(AUDIENCE LAUGH)
-Now, as it happens,

00:03:42.188 --> 00:03:44.656
the judge he initially insulted
is overseeing cases

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:47.426
involving the controversial
Trump University.

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:48.994
And he ordered
a cache of documents

00:03:49.094 --> 00:03:50.562
to be released this week.

00:03:50.763 --> 00:03:51.998
Which was very exciting to us,

00:03:52.098 --> 00:03:54.066
because we actually
looked into his university

00:03:54.166 --> 00:03:55.768
when we did our big piece
on Trump

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:56.869
back in February,

00:03:56.969 --> 00:03:59.271
and it wound up
on this very long list

00:03:59.371 --> 00:04:00.940
of awful Donald Trump stories

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:03.542
that we literally
didn't have time to delve into,

00:04:03.642 --> 00:04:05.744
even in a 22-minute piece.

00:04:06.011 --> 00:04:09.548
But, once we started reading
through these new documents,

00:04:09.648 --> 00:04:11.250
we figured, "Aw, fuck it.

00:04:11.350 --> 00:04:13.386
Let's take some time
to talk about it now."

00:04:13.486 --> 00:04:15.721
-(AUDIENCE LAUGH)
-Because Trump University

00:04:15.821 --> 00:04:17.456
is kind of amazing.

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:20.793
Back when it opened,
Trump made some big claims.

00:04:20.893 --> 00:04:23.329
At Trump University,
we teach success.

00:04:23.529 --> 00:04:25.798
That's what it's all about,
success.

00:04:25.898 --> 00:04:27.332
It's going to happen to you.

00:04:27.566 --> 00:04:28.934
If you don't learn
from the people

00:04:29.034 --> 00:04:30.436
that we're going to be
putting forward,

00:04:30.536 --> 00:04:33.406
and these are all people
that are handpicked by me,

00:04:33.973 --> 00:04:35.375
then, uh,
you're just not gonna make it

00:04:35.475 --> 00:04:37.243
in terms of
the world of success.

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:40.379
(SCOFFS)
"The world of success."

00:04:40.846 --> 00:04:42.314
It sounds like
what Donald Trump

00:04:42.414 --> 00:04:43.883
-calls his bedroom.
-(AUDIENCE LAUGH)

00:04:43.983 --> 00:04:45.751
"Welcome to
The World of Success.

00:04:46.051 --> 00:04:48.954
Please enjoy a mint,
and a nondisclosure agreement."

00:04:49.054 --> 00:04:51.190
-(AUDIENCE LAUGH)
-Now, unfortunately,

00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:53.726
Trump University ran into
problems in several states,

00:04:53.826 --> 00:04:55.561
starting with the name itself.

00:04:55.995 --> 00:04:57.896 line:0%
We started looking at
Trump University,

00:04:58.130 --> 00:04:59.932 line:0%
and, uh, discovered that it was

00:05:00.032 --> 00:05:01.700 line:0%
a classic
bait-and-switch scheme.

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:03.068 line:0%
It was a scam.

00:05:03.502 --> 00:05:05.371 line:0%
Starting with the fact that
it was not a university.

00:05:05.705 --> 00:05:06.772
Holy shit!

00:05:07.173 --> 00:05:10.109
Trump University
wasn't even a university.

00:05:10.409 --> 00:05:11.778
Which is enough
to make you wonder

00:05:11.878 --> 00:05:13.746
what the fuck
was in Trump steaks?

00:05:13.846 --> 00:05:15.681
Oh God, it was possum,
wasn't it?

00:05:15.781 --> 00:05:17.816
It was possum, you monsters!

00:05:17.916 --> 00:05:19.084
(AUDIENCE LAUGH)

00:05:19.384 --> 00:05:21.387
But the name
was just the beginning,

00:05:21.487 --> 00:05:24.356
'cause remember how he had
"handpicked instructors"?

00:05:24.456 --> 00:05:26.358
Well, according to
his own depositions,

00:05:26.458 --> 00:05:29.261
he did not personally select
instructors for live seminars,

00:05:29.495 --> 00:05:31.397
and was unable
to recall the names

00:05:31.497 --> 00:05:32.832
of key faculty members.

00:05:33.098 --> 00:05:35.835
And it's probably good that
he didn't handpick them himself,

00:05:36.035 --> 00:05:37.036
that would be dangerous.

00:05:37.270 --> 00:05:39.404
Anything
Trump's tiny fingers touch

00:05:39.505 --> 00:05:42.207
turn into an ex-wife
or an abandoned casino.

00:05:42.307 --> 00:05:44.844
And it doesn't stop there.

00:05:44.944 --> 00:05:48.080
According to the sworn testimony
by several former employees,

00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:51.416
many instructors and mentors
had no experience

00:05:51.717 --> 00:05:53.419
buying or selling real estate.

00:05:53.519 --> 00:05:56.288
In fact, one had worked
as a salesmen for Lowe's,

00:05:56.555 --> 00:05:59.358
and another had been manager
for Buffalo Wild Wings.

00:05:59.458 --> 00:06:02.161
-(AUDIENCE LAUGH)
-Or as I call it, B-dubs-dubs.

00:06:02.461 --> 00:06:05.198
-(AUDIENCE LAUGH)
-And even a former member

00:06:05.298 --> 00:06:07.900
of Trump's own sale's staff
testified that it was,

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:10.536
among other things,
a joke, a facade,

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:13.272
and was just selling
false hopes and lies.

00:06:13.572 --> 00:06:17.510
And to be fair, every university
has sold some of its students

00:06:17.610 --> 00:06:20.113
false hopes and lies.
It's just, most of the time,

00:06:20.213 --> 00:06:21.948
they call it
"a theater arts degree."

00:06:22.048 --> 00:06:24.784
-(AUDIENCE LAUGH)
-Now, these new documents

00:06:25.017 --> 00:06:29.589
also include several revealing
playbooks of sales tactics.

00:06:29.689 --> 00:06:31.190
For instance,
the room temperature

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:34.126
was to be no more
than 68 degrees,

00:06:34.226 --> 00:06:36.128
which is partly
to keep students alert,

00:06:36.228 --> 00:06:38.263
and partly because
Professor Wild Wings

00:06:38.364 --> 00:06:40.499
doesn't want the ranch sauce
getting all gamy.

00:06:40.699 --> 00:06:42.702
-(AUDIENCE LAUGH)
-There are also instructions

00:06:42.802 --> 00:06:45.004
on how to sell
and upsell students,

00:06:45.104 --> 00:06:48.941
or as the playbooks call them,
"buyers", on expensive courses,

00:06:49.041 --> 00:06:51.077
with typo-riddled tips like,

00:06:51.177 --> 00:06:53.545
"If a client is adamant
about knowing the price,

00:06:53.812 --> 00:06:59.752
simply say, 'Our course range
anywhere from $29 to $35,000.'"

00:07:00.019 --> 00:07:01.887
And if prospects
seemed at all wary,

00:07:01.987 --> 00:07:03.722
there was advice
for dealing with that.

00:07:04.289 --> 00:07:06.191 line:0%
MAN:
<i>'"You must be very aggressive,"</i>

00:07:06.291 --> 00:07:08.260 line:0%
<i> one passage
 from the playbook reads.</i>

00:07:08.460 --> 00:07:10.062 line:0%
<i> '"If they complain
 about the price,</i>

00:07:10.262 --> 00:07:12.865 line:0%
<i> remind them
 that Trump is the best."</i>

00:07:13.232 --> 00:07:14.967
-(AUDIENCE LAUGH)
-You might laugh,

00:07:15.067 --> 00:07:17.236
but that is the same technique
that Trump has been using

00:07:17.336 --> 00:07:18.871
to run for president,
and apparently,

00:07:18.971 --> 00:07:21.407
-it fucking works!
-(AUDIENCE LAUGH)

00:07:21.640 --> 00:07:24.744
These playbooks are rife
with sleazy salesmanship.

00:07:24.844 --> 00:07:27.480
For instance, employees were
told to substitute the words

00:07:27.713 --> 00:07:30.249
"thank you"
with "congratulations",

00:07:30.349 --> 00:07:33.251
so that the potential costumer
ends up thanking you.

00:07:34.019 --> 00:07:36.589
-Which is pretty obnoxious.
-(AUDIENCE LAUGH)

00:07:36.689 --> 00:07:38.857
If I started this show
every week with,

00:07:38.957 --> 00:07:42.428
"Welcome to<i> Last Week Tonight,</i>
congratulations on joining us,"

00:07:42.528 --> 00:07:44.363
you would quite rightly
turn it off.

00:07:44.463 --> 00:07:45.431
(AUDIENCE LAUGH)

00:07:45.531 --> 00:07:46.499
And I know what
you're thinking,

00:07:46.599 --> 00:07:47.667
"Well, what about people

00:07:47.767 --> 00:07:49.401
who simply
didn't have the money?"

00:07:49.768 --> 00:07:52.404
Trump U didn't really
have a problem with that.

00:07:53.005 --> 00:07:54.773 line:0%
MAN:<i> A set of playbooks
 for the sales team</i>

00:07:54.874 --> 00:07:56.909 line:0%
<i> coached them on
 how to market the courses,</i>

00:07:57.009 --> 00:07:59.712 line:0%
<i> even to single mothers
with three children who, quote,</i>

00:07:59.812 --> 00:08:01.446 line:0%
<i> "may need money for food."</i>

00:08:01.546 --> 00:08:03.281 line:0%
<i> "Money,"
 instructed the playbook,</i>

00:08:03.381 --> 00:08:05.818
<i> "is never a reason for not
 enrolling in Trump University.</i>

00:08:05.918 --> 00:08:07.720
<i> If they real believe in you
 and your product,</i>

00:08:07.820 --> 00:08:08.854
<i> they will find the money.</i>

00:08:09.188 --> 00:08:10.923
<i> You are not doing any favor
 by letting someone</i>

00:08:11.023 --> 00:08:13.558
<i> use lack of money
 as an excuse."</i>

00:08:14.092 --> 00:08:16.162
"Lack of money
is not an excuse"

00:08:16.395 --> 00:08:18.397
is not what single parents
need to hear.

00:08:18.630 --> 00:08:20.366
It's what Donald Trump
needs to hear

00:08:20.466 --> 00:08:21.901
when a fifth company of his

00:08:22.001 --> 00:08:24.536
inevitably files
for Chapter 11 bankruptcy.

00:08:24.970 --> 00:08:26.905
And as you might expect,

00:08:27.005 --> 00:08:29.474
some of the customers on
the other end of that hard sell

00:08:29.575 --> 00:08:31.944
wound up feeling duped,
like Carmen Mendez,

00:08:32.044 --> 00:08:35.380
who put a $35,000 course
on her credit cards

00:08:35.480 --> 00:08:36.782
and was left disappointed.

00:08:37.249 --> 00:08:39.252 line:0%
CARMEN:<i> I thought that
I'm going to be a millionaire...</i>

00:08:40.286 --> 00:08:42.955 line:0%
because Donald Trump
is a millionaire

00:08:43.055 --> 00:08:44.723 line:0%
and they were
offering the course

00:08:44.823 --> 00:08:46.958 line:0%
for people to get rich.

00:08:47.693 --> 00:08:50.830 line:0%
MAN:<i> This is the closest Mendez
got to Trump during the course,</i>

00:08:51.197 --> 00:08:54.200 line:0%
<i> a picture of her
with a picture of Donald Trump.</i>

00:08:54.533 --> 00:08:56.768
Oh, that's not a one-off,

00:08:57.035 --> 00:08:58.537
'cause another
former student said,

00:08:58.637 --> 00:08:59.972
"We were told that
we would get to have

00:09:00.072 --> 00:09:01.973
our pictures taken
with Donald Trump.

00:09:02.240 --> 00:09:05.611
It ended up being a cardboard
cutout of Mr. Trump."

00:09:06.211 --> 00:09:09.848
Which is actually a perfect
metaphor for Trump University.

00:09:10.048 --> 00:09:12.218
You're expecting the real thing,
but in the end,

00:09:12.318 --> 00:09:14.687
all you get is a tacky,
two-dimensional facade

00:09:14.787 --> 00:09:16.688
with Donald Trump's face
slapped on it.

00:09:16.788 --> 00:09:17.789
(AUDIENCE LAUGH)

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:20.426
But perhaps
the most suspicious thing of all

00:09:20.526 --> 00:09:23.662
is that the playbooks even
include specific instructions

00:09:23.895 --> 00:09:26.599
on what to do if an
attorney general shows up.

00:09:26.699 --> 00:09:29.167
And believe it or not,
the answer is not,

00:09:29.267 --> 00:09:30.803
"Kick over a table
as a distraction

00:09:30.903 --> 00:09:32.905
-and get the fuck out of there."
-(AUDIENCE LAUGH)

00:09:33.005 --> 00:09:36.608
No, apparently you contact April
immediately.

00:09:36.808 --> 00:09:38.811
-(AUDIENCE LAUGH)
-And it also reminds you,

00:09:38.911 --> 00:09:41.413
"You do not have to show them
any personal information

00:09:41.513 --> 00:09:42.915
unless they have a warrant."

00:09:43.282 --> 00:09:45.084
Which is suspicious advice

00:09:45.351 --> 00:09:47.919
-for a university employee.
-(AUDIENCE LAUGH)

00:09:48.019 --> 00:09:50.555
I'm pretty sure Harvard
doesn't tell its new professors,

00:09:50.656 --> 00:09:53.092
"Welcome, here's a gun
and a cyanide capsule

00:09:53.192 --> 00:09:54.460
in case the fuzz show up.

00:09:54.560 --> 00:09:57.162
-Don't let them take you alive!"
-(AUDIENCE LAUGH)

00:09:57.730 --> 00:10:00.232
-Now, Donald Trump...
-(AUDIENCE APPLAUD)

00:10:00.332 --> 00:10:04.302
Donald Trump has broadly denied
the claims in the lawsuits,

00:10:04.402 --> 00:10:06.238
and his attorneys
have gathered statements

00:10:06.338 --> 00:10:07.739
from satisfied customers.

00:10:07.840 --> 00:10:09.442
In fact, to hear Trump tell it,

00:10:09.542 --> 00:10:11.176
"The school
was very good value."

00:10:11.443 --> 00:10:13.345 line:0%
Ninety-eight percent
of the people

00:10:13.445 --> 00:10:14.413 line:0%
that took the courses--

00:10:14.513 --> 00:10:16.181 line:0%
we have report cards
from everybody.

00:10:16.515 --> 00:10:18.517 line:0%
They report-carded
on the course.

00:10:18.617 --> 00:10:20.219 line:0%
Ninety-eight percent
of the people

00:10:20.319 --> 00:10:21.587 line:0%
that took the courses,

00:10:21.687 --> 00:10:23.121 line:0%
ninety-eight percent
approved the courses,

00:10:23.221 --> 00:10:24.456 line:0%
they thought they were terrific.

00:10:24.923 --> 00:10:29.228
Okay, first there is something
instantly fishy about 98%.

00:10:29.661 --> 00:10:32.331
The only things that have that
level of unanimous approval

00:10:32.431 --> 00:10:33.532
are dictators,

00:10:33.632 --> 00:10:35.934
Pixar movies,
and Neapolitan ice cream.

00:10:36.034 --> 00:10:37.035
(AUDIENCE LAUGH)

00:10:37.236 --> 00:10:38.871
Yeah, it's got chocolate
for the chocoholics,

00:10:38.971 --> 00:10:41.540
vanilla for the borings,
and strawberry for the perverts.

00:10:41.740 --> 00:10:43.843
-(AUDIENCE LAUGH)
-In fact,

00:10:44.243 --> 00:10:45.744
according to plaintiffs,

00:10:46.144 --> 00:10:48.013
the reason those numbers
are so high

00:10:48.113 --> 00:10:50.149
is because the surveys
were not anonymous

00:10:50.249 --> 00:10:51.851
and were filled out
when participants

00:10:51.951 --> 00:10:55.086
were still expecting to receive
future benefits from the program

00:10:55.187 --> 00:10:57.189
such as assistance or mentoring

00:10:57.289 --> 00:10:59.457
from the instructor
they were evaluating.

00:10:59.658 --> 00:11:02.027
So listen to why
one former student

00:11:02.127 --> 00:11:04.163
gave it a good review
that he now regrets.

00:11:04.930 --> 00:11:06.432 line:0%
I really look at it like this,

00:11:06.532 --> 00:11:07.533 line:0%
is... is...

00:11:07.733 --> 00:11:09.335 line:0%
Say you go to
a really nice restaurant.

00:11:10.569 --> 00:11:11.671 line:0%
And, uh...

00:11:12.371 --> 00:11:13.439 line:0%
really expensive restaurant,

00:11:13.539 --> 00:11:15.040 line:0%
you eat this
really gorgeous dinner,

00:11:15.140 --> 00:11:16.775 line:0%
and the chef comes out
near the end of your meal,

00:11:16.875 --> 00:11:18.243 line:0%
and asks you
how you liked the meal,

00:11:18.343 --> 00:11:19.778 line:0%
and you really, really loved it.

00:11:20.145 --> 00:11:21.947 line:0%
But then you--
by the time you go home,

00:11:22.247 --> 00:11:24.616 line:0%
you realize that, uh,
you've gotten food poisoning

00:11:24.717 --> 00:11:25.851 line:0%
and you're really, really sick.

00:11:26.085 --> 00:11:27.519 line:0%
INTERVIEWER: What do you think
about Trump University?

00:11:27.620 --> 00:11:28.920 line:0%
I feel like I've been poisoned.

00:11:29.654 --> 00:11:31.323 line:0%
I just felt like
I was just duped,

00:11:31.423 --> 00:11:32.625 line:0%
and poisoned, and ripped off.

00:11:33.325 --> 00:11:35.994
The only thing worse than that
is having that same feeling

00:11:36.094 --> 00:11:38.029
and then realizing,
"Oh, shit!

00:11:38.129 --> 00:11:41.966
He's got three years, 364 days,
left in his first term."

00:11:42.067 --> 00:11:43.702
-(AUDIENCE GROAN)
-But perhaps

00:11:43.802 --> 00:11:46.472
the most valuable lesson
to come out of Trump University

00:11:46.572 --> 00:11:48.874
is the one that
it is currently giving all of us

00:11:48.974 --> 00:11:51.843
in what's behind
Trump's campaign strategy.

00:11:52.044 --> 00:11:54.046
Because the playbook
tells his salespeople,

00:11:54.146 --> 00:11:57.149
"You don't sell products,
benefits or solutions,

00:11:57.416 --> 00:11:58.617
you sell feelings."

00:11:58.850 --> 00:12:01.019
And that
is what is happening now.

00:12:01.319 --> 00:12:03.088
Crowds at a Trump rally
may not be able

00:12:03.188 --> 00:12:05.791
to point to a concrete benefit
or solution he offers,

00:12:05.991 --> 00:12:08.393
but they know
how he makes them feel,

00:12:08.693 --> 00:12:11.463
and that is jacked up
and ready to boo any name

00:12:11.563 --> 00:12:13.198
that sounds vaguely Latino.

00:12:13.298 --> 00:12:14.299
(AUDIENCE LAUGH)

00:12:14.699 --> 00:12:16.635
So if you are planning
to vote for Trump in November,

00:12:16.735 --> 00:12:18.604
I'd like to direct you
to a quote from the top

00:12:18.704 --> 00:12:20.973
of Trump University's
old homepage,

00:12:21.340 --> 00:12:23.776
"Take the risk,
but before you do,

00:12:23.876 --> 00:12:25.677
learn what
you're getting yourself into."

00:12:26.078 --> 00:12:28.914
Donald, I could not
have said it better myself.

00:12:29.014 --> 00:12:30.482
-(AUDIENCE LAUGH)
-So thank you.

00:12:30.582 --> 00:12:33.219
Or should I say,
"Congratulations"?

